## [v0.4.7] — 2026-04-18 API cleanup, deprecation removal, and fitting performance

### Changed
- Backend resolution and fallback-reason assembly consolidated into one canonical path in
  `ramanspy_bridge.py`; redundant double key-set for the native branch removed.
- Preprocessing normalisation centralised in `preprocessing.py`: added
  `canonicalize_baseline_spec()`, `canonicalize_pipeline_steps()`, and
  `normalize_backend_request()` as the single entry points for all callers.
- `BaselineSubtract` now normalises its `baseline_spec` in `__post_init__` (not on every
  `apply()` call); `_resolve_savgol_params_for_mapping` unified with `_resolve_savgol_params`.
- `exporter.py` is now the single owner of provenance serialisation: added
  `serialize_preprocessing_provenance()` for extracting canonical recipe fields from
  preprocessing result metadata.
- All five `BaselineAPI.parse_spec()` call-sites migrated to `baseline_spec_to_runtime()`
  from `schema.py` (`_preprocess.py`, `_pl_mapping.py` ×2, `_raman_mapping.py` ×2).
- `batch.py` provenance assembly now routes through `serialise_backend_provenance()` instead
  of manual field extraction.

### Removed

- `poly_degree` parameter from `RamanFit` and `PLfit` (hard removed; callers get
  `TypeError: unexpected keyword argument`).
- `BaselineAPI.parse_spec()` (hard removed; was `FutureWarning`-deprecated).
- `resolve_baseline_method_with_deprecation()` and `POLY_DEGREE_SENTINEL` from
  `single_fit/_single_fit_core.py`.
- `_validate_raman_axis()` from `ramanspy_adapter.py` (duplicate policy enforcement;
  callers now call `can_use_ramanspy()` directly).
- Local fallback provenance construction from `mapping/_preprocess.py`; bridge always
  returns a canonical dict so the fallback path was dead code.

### Fixed

- **Fitting performance regression (v0.4.5+):** `RamanFit.__init__()` was calling
  `resolve_preprocessing_backend()` on every construction, which internally called
  `has_ramanspy()`. On a cold Python session (ramanspy not yet imported), this
  triggered a ~3.5 s ramanspy cold-import even when `preprocessing_backend='native'`.
  Fixed in two places:
  - `ramanspy_adapter.py`: `has_ramanspy()` now uses `@lru_cache(maxsize=1)` so the
    result is cached after the first probe; all subsequent calls cost ~0 µs.
  - `ramanspy_bridge.py`: `resolve_preprocessing_backend()` short-circuits immediately
    for `backend='native'` before calling `has_ramanspy()`, eliminating the probe
    entirely for all native-backend workflows.
  - Affected workflows: `RamanFit`, `PLfit` (single-spectrum), `PLMapping`, and
    `RamanMapping` with `preprocessing_backend='native'`. `PLMapping` always uses
    native, so it is fully covered; confirmed via profiling that no ramanspy probe
    occurs at any point in the PLMapping construction or preprocessing path.
  - Measured improvement: `RamanFit.__init__()` drops from ~33 ms to ~1 ms
    (warm-session, single-peak 300-point spectrum).
- `FutureWarning` no longer emitted from `make_compat_data_importer()` on default
  `readlines`; stripped warning-only code path.
- `poly_degree` key no longer appears in exported metadata.

### Added

- `peak_models.py`: `sum_peaks_jac_lorentzian()` — vectorised analytical Jacobian
  for the Lorentzian peak sum; eliminates finite-difference derivative evaluations
  during `scipy.optimize.curve_fit` iterations.
- `RamanFit.fit_spectrum()` and `PLfit.fit_spectrum()`: new `maxfev` parameter
  (default 6400, unchanged) so callers can reduce the evaluation budget for
  well-conditioned warm-start fits (e.g. `maxfev=1600`). Lorentzian fits
  automatically pass the analytical Jacobian via `self._jac`.

### Tests

- Added: `tests/test_preprocessing_spec_normalization.py` (17 tests)
- Added: `tests/test_backend_resolution_contract.py` (8 tests + 1 skipped)
- Added: `tests/test_backend_error_messages.py` (6 tests + 1 skipped)
- Added: `tests/test_provenance_serialization.py` (12 tests)
- Added: `tests/test_deprecation_removals.py` (7 tests)
- Updated: `tests/test_single_fit_regressions.py` — removed two tests for deleted functions.
- Updated: `tests/test_export_provenance_regressions.py` — migrated two tests to use
  canonical `_preprocess_meta` structure instead of direct attribute assignment.

### Docs

- `README.md`: added "Preprocessing & Backend Contract" section documenting backend
  selection semantics, which workflows are RamanSPy-capable, and canonical provenance fields.

## [v0.4.6] — 2026-04-17 Performance profiling and baseline optimisation

### Optimised
- `baselineAPI.py` — `asLS`, `arPLS`, `airPLS`: extracted shared `_whittaker_diff_matrix()`
  helper to deduplicate difference-operator construction across all three methods. Added
  `_DtD_cache` (module-level dict) and `_get_cached_DtD(n, diff_order)` so `D^T D` is
  computed once per `(n, diff_order)` key and reused across all calls. Pre-computed
  `lam * DtD` (and for airPLS, `ridge * I`) before each method's iteration loop so that
  only `W` and `Z` are rebuilt per iteration. Eliminates `O(niter)` sparse matrix products
  per spectrum; gain is proportional to `niter` and spectrum length.

### Added
- `benchmarks/benchmark_baseline_kernels.py` (new): microbenchmark sweeping spectrum length
  (128, 512, 1024) across all five native baseline methods. Records runtime and peak memory.
  Does not test scientific correctness — see `test_baseline_numerical_parity.py` for that.
- Extended `benchmarks/benchmark_mapping_preprocessing.py` with two additional dataset sizes:
  `extended_30x30` (150-point axis) and `tall_axis_10x12` (500-point axis).
- `tests/test_baseline_numerical_parity.py` (new): 11 tests verifying asLS, arPLS, airPLS
  numerical output against reference implementations within `atol=1e-10`.
- `tests/test_baseline_operator_cache.py` (new): 9 tests covering cache identity, keying,
  numerical correctness, and `_whittaker_diff_matrix` shape/correctness.
- `tests/test_batch_performance_path_regressions.py` (new): 4 batch regression tests
  confirming fit output, summary table shape, and provenance fields are unchanged after
  lower-level baseline optimisation.
- `tests/test_mapping_backend_parity.py`: added two native self-consistency tests
  (`asLS`, `arPLS`) confirming the DtD cache does not cause state mutation between calls.
- `tests/test_mapping_cube_consistency.py`: added cube shape + finite-values test for asLS
  preprocessing via the DtD-cached path.

### Changed
- `integration/ramanspy_adapter.py`: added inline comment documenting that the `[Y,X,N] →
  [X,Y,N]` transpose is unavoidable (conversion overhead not further reducible in this build).
- `README.md` repository structure section corrected to reflect actual source layout: fixed
  `single_fit/` filenames (`RamanFit.py`, `PLfit.py`), removed non-existent `data_importer/`
  subpackage, added missing top-level modules (`dataImporter.py`, `peak_models.py`, `schema.py`,
  `raman_materials.json`), added missing `mapping/` modules (`_diagnostics.py`, `_fit_utils.py`,
  `_image.py`), noted compatibility façades, listed all 15 test files, and updated benchmarks
  section to include `benchmark_baseline_kernels.py`.

### Notes
- Scientific behaviour and public API are unchanged.
- Gains are strongest for `asLS`/`arPLS` on long spectra or large mapping cubes (20+ iterations
  eliminated per spectrum call).
- `airPLS` already pre-computed `DtD` per-call before v0.4.6; now additionally pre-computes
  `lam * DtD + ridge * I` before the loop and uses the cross-call cache.
- `preprocessing.py` per-spectrum loop is already copy-minimal for float64 cubes (audited).
- API/deprecation cleanup and new preprocessing algorithms remain deferred to v0.4.7.

---------

## [v0.4.5] — 2026-04-16 Backend API cleanup and provenance hardening

### Added
- `resolve_backend_outcome()` in `integration/ramanspy_bridge.py`: canonical backend
  decision function that combines availability checks, input compatibility, and pipeline
  translation support into a single outcome dict with fields `fallback_used`,
  `fallback_reason`, and `failure_mode`. Replaces scattered per-caller decision logic.
- `format_backend_fallback_reason()` and `format_backend_error_message()` helpers in
  `ramanspy_bridge.py` for consistent user-facing message generation.
- `inspect_pipeline_backend_support()` in `preprocessing.py`: public helper that inspects
  a pipeline's translation support without committing to a full backend resolution.
- `serialise_backend_provenance()` in `exporter.py`: single shared helper that extracts the
  stable public subset (`preprocessing_backend_requested`, `preprocessing_backend_resolved`,
  optionally `preprocessing_backend_fallback_reason`) from a canonical outcome dict.
- `BACKEND_OUTCOME_REQUIRED_KEYS` frozenset and `validate_backend_outcome_keys()` in
  `schema.py` to guard against outcome dict key drift.
- `_backend_outcome` attribute on `RamanFit` and `PLfit` fitter objects (alias for
  `preprocessing_backend_info`) giving all callers a stable provenance handle.
- New test files:
  - `tests/test_backend_message_consistency.py` (12 tests): fallback/error wording stable
    across auto/forced ramanspy scenarios; message helper unit tests.
  - `tests/test_backend_provenance_consistency.py` (14 tests): serialisation consistency,
    pipeline support summary, schema guard.
  - `tests/test_single_fit_backend_meta.py` (6 tests): fitter `_backend_outcome` attribute
    correctness, export metadata provenance fields.

### Changed
- `_resolve_pipeline_backend_for_input()` in `preprocessing.py` refactored to a thin
  wrapper: calls `pipeline_supports_ramanspy_translation()` then delegates the full
  decision to `resolve_backend_outcome()`. All decision logic now lives in one place.
- `build_single_fit_export_metadata()` in `_single_fit_core.py` now calls
  `serialise_backend_provenance()` when `_backend_outcome` is available, providing
  consistent provenance keys in single-fit exports.
- `_build_mapping_fit_export_meta()` in `mapping/_preprocess.py` now reads
  `preprocessing_backend_info` from `_preprocess_meta` and uses
  `serialise_backend_provenance()` instead of assembling provenance fields directly.
  Mapping exports now correctly reflect the resolved backend after preprocessing runs.
- `_infer_metadata_from_fitters()` in `batch.py` now additionally extracts
  `preprocessing_backend_fallback_reason` from fitter `_backend_outcome` objects.

### Fixed
- Mapping exports previously always wrote `preprocessing_backend_resolved: null` because
  `self.preprocessing_backend_resolved` was never updated after preprocessing. Now reads
  the resolved backend from `_preprocess_meta["preprocessing_backend_info"]` via the
  shared serialiser.
- Inconsistent fallback reason wording: previously only set in some paths, now produced
  by a single `_build_auto_fallback_reason()` helper for all callers.
- `preprocessing_backend_fallback_reason` absent from batch and single-fit exports even
  when auto fallback occurred. Now emitted consistently by `serialise_backend_provenance()`.

### Notes
- No new analysis features, no PL RamanSPy expansion, no performance work.
- All plotting, table, and numerical preprocessing behaviour is unchanged.
- 77 tests pass (47 existing + 30 new).

